 "seiten": {
  "cc0": "<link rel='shortlink' href='https://godotshaders.com/?p=17403' />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://godotshaders.com/shader/light-enabled-3d-color-palette-material/\" />\n<article id=\"post-17403\" class=\"entry content-bg single-entry post-17403 shader type-shader status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry godot_version-godot_version_44 shader_license-cc0 shader_tag-3d shader_tag-color shader_tag-color-palette shader_tag-light shader_tag-palette shader_tag-surface shader_type-spatial\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\">Light Enabled 3D Color Palette Material</h1>\n<span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://godotshaders.com/author/literallyanyone/\">LiterallyAnyone</a></span>\n<pre class=\"line-numbers code-block\"><code class=\"language-glsl\">// NOTE: Transparent pipeline does not like multiple light sources.\r\n\r\n// from light pre-pass\r\nshader_type spatial;\r\nrender_mode blend_mix,depth_draw_always;\r\n\r\n\r\nuniform sampler2D texture_albedo : filter_nearest, repeat_enable;\r\nuniform vec3 uv1_scale;\r\nuniform vec3 uv1_offset;\r\n\r\nuniform sampler2D texture_normal: hint_roughness_normal, filter_nearest, repeat_enable;\r\nuniform vec2 normal_scale = vec2(1.0);\r\nuniform vec2 normal_offset = vec2(0.0);\r\n\r\n\r\n// from color applicator\r\nconst float lin = .45454545;\r\nconst float srgb = 2.2;\r\n\r\nuniform float rows = 4.0;\r\nuniform float cols = 32.0;\r\n\r\nuniform sampler2D pal:  filter_nearest;\r\nuniform float dither_size = 1;\r\nuniform float dither_amount: hint_range(0.0, 1.0);\r\n\r\nuniform float palette_power = 4.0;\r\n\r\nfloat lerp(float val1, float val2, float mul) {\r</code></pre>\n</article>",
  "mit": "<link rel='shortlink' href='https://godotshaders.com/?p=17380' />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://godotshaders.com/shader/laser-and-lightning-beam/\" />\n<article id=\"post-17380\" class=\"entry content-bg single-entry post-17380 shader type-shader status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry godot_version-godot_version_44 godot_version-4-7 shader_license-mit shader_tag-3d shader_tag-beam shader_tag-electric shader_tag-energy shader_tag-laser shader_tag-lightning shader_tag-magic shader_tag-sci-fi shader_tag-vfx shader_tag-zigzag shader_type-spatial shader_version-gles3\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\">Laser and Lightning Beam</h1>\n<span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://godotshaders.com/author/gennai/\">gennai</a></span>\n<pre class=\"line-numbers code-block\"><code class=\"language-glsl\">// Lightning / Laser Beam for Godot 4\r\n// MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 gennai (https://gennai.itch.io)\r\n//\r\n// A glowing beam on one thin strip. Put this on a MeshInstance3D with a long, thin\r\n// QuadMesh (for example size 8 x 0.6) as Geometry &gt; Material Override. UV.x runs\r\n// along the beam, UV.y across it. With face_camera on, the strip turns around its\r\n// long axis to face the camera, so it never shows edge-on.\r\n//\r\n// Animate appear from 0 to 1 to shoot the beam out, then vanish from 0 to 1 to\r\n// pull it back in. Set jag_amount to 0 for a straight laser, and raise it for a jagged lightning bolt.\r\n// No textures: the noise is computed in the shader and looks the same on every renderer.\r\nshader_type spatial;\r\nrender_mode unshaded, blend_add, depth_draw_never, cull_disabled, skip_vertex_transform, shadows_disabled, fog_disabled;\r\n\r\ngroup_uniforms timing;\r\n// 0 = no beam, 1 = beam reaches the far end. Animate this to fire it.\r\nuniform float appear : hint_range(0.0, 1.0) = 1.0;\r\n// 0 = beam intact, 1 = the tail has caught up and the beam is gone.\r\nuniform float vanish : hint_range(0.0, 1.0) = 0.0;\r\n// Fade length at both ends, as a fraction of the beam length.\r\nuniform float end_fade : hint_range(0.0, 0.5) = 0.08;\r\n\r\ngroup_uniforms shape;\r\n// Turn the strip around its long axis to face the camera.\r\nuniform bool face_camera = true;\r\n// Thickness of the bright core, as a fraction of the strip width.\r\nuniform float core_width : hint_range(0.02, 1.0) = 0.14;\r\n// How quickly the outer glow fades out. Higher = tighter glow.\r\nuniform float glow_falloff : hint_range(0.5, 8.0) = 2.0;\r\n// How far the path swings sideways, as a fraction of the strip half-width. 0 = straight laser.\r</code></pre>\n</article>",
  "gnu_gpl3": "<link rel='shortlink' href='https://godotshaders.com/?p=13966' />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://godotshaders.com/shader/bubble-glass-spatial-shader-with-chromatic-aberration-and-homemade-rim-lighting/\" />\n<article id=\"post-13966\" class=\"entry content-bg single-entry post-13966 shader type-shader status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry shader_license-gnu_gpl3 shader_tag-bubbles shader_tag-chromatic-aberration shader_tag-glass shader_type-spatial\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\">Bubble/Glass spatial shader with chromatic aberration</h1>\n<span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://godotshaders.com/author/giwbyalbatross/\">GiwbyAlbatross</a></span>\n<pre class=\"line-numbers code-block\"><code class=\"language-glsl\">shader_type spatial;\r\nrender_mode unshaded;\r\n\r\n/* Bubble or Glass shader, best applied to spheres.\r\n * It is not affected by lighting in the scene, only whatever&#039;s behind it.\r\n * \r\n * Set rim_lightness to 0.0 to be more glass and less bubble.\r\n * Set it to 0.6 for full Good Witch Of The North vibes.\r\n * \r\n * Setting chromatic_aberration to 0.0 removes the effect (no performance difference).\r\n * It gets ridiculous if you set it past around 0.25.\r\n * \r\n * Warping affects the degree to which the backdrop is warped (not technically accurate).\r\n * \r\n * Greyness is effectively a contrast control for whatever&#039;s behind it.\r\n * 0.0 is full contrast, 1.0 is pure 0.5 grey.\r\n *\r\n * Should be compatitable with Godot Engine 3 and 4.\r\n */\r\n\r\n// comment out for godot &gt;=4.0\r\n#define OLD_GODOT\r\n\r\nuniform float chromatic_aberration = 0.01;\r\nuniform float warping = 0.1;\r\nuniform float greyness = 0.2;\r\nuniform float rim_lightness = 0.15;\r\n\r\n#ifndef OLD_GODOT\r\nuniform sampler2D SCREEN_TEXTURE: hint_screen_texture;\r</code></pre>\n</article>",
  "shadertoy_port": "<link rel='shortlink' href='https://godotshaders.com/?p=15136' />\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://godotshaders.com/shader/vhs-4/\" />\n<article id=\"post-15136\" class=\"entry content-bg single-entry post-15136 shader type-shader status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry godot_version-godot_version_36 godot_version-godot_version_36-2 godot_version-godot_version_37 godot_version-godot_version_40 godot_version-godot_version_41 godot_version-godot_version_42 godot_version-godot_version_43 godot_version-godot_version_44 godot_version-godot_version_45 godot_version-godot_version_46 shader_license-shadertoy_port shader_tag-vhs shader_type-canvas_item shader_version-gles2 shader_version-gles3\">\n<h1 class=\"entry-title\">vhs</h1>\n<span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://godotshaders.com/author/cvc/\">cvc</a></span>\n<pre class=\"line-numbers code-block\"><code class=\"language-glsl\">shader_type canvas_item;\r\n\r\nuniform sampler2D SCREEN_TEXTURE : hint_screen_texture, filter_linear_mipmap;\r\n\r\n// --- UPDATED AESTHETIC PARAMETERS ---\r\nuniform float color_levels : hint_range(2.0, 128.0) = 14.0;\r\nuniform float chromatic_aberration : hint_range(0.0, 0.2) = 0.008;\r\nuniform float blur_amount : hint_range(0.0, 5.0) = 1.0;\r\nuniform float brightness : hint_range(0.5, 3.0) = 1.2;\r\nuniform float saturation : hint_range(1.0, 5.0) = 1.0;\r\n\r\n// --- UPDATED GLITCH PARAMETERS ---\r\nuniform float color_offset_multiplier: hint_range(0.0, 0.2) = 0.004;\r\nuniform float black_offset_multiplier: hint_range(0.0, 0.5) = 0.1;\r\nuniform float color_offset: hint_range(-0.1, 0.1) = 0.005;\r\n\r\n// Noise function\r\nfloat noise(vec2 uv, float offset) {\r\n\treturn (fract(sin(dot(uv * offset, vec2(12.9898, 78.233))) * 43758.5453) - 0.5) * 2.0;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvec3 rgb_to_yuv(vec3 rgb) {\r\n\tconst mat3 RGB_TO_YUV = mat3(vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114), vec3(-0.14713, -0.28886, 0.436), vec3(.615, -0.51499, -0.10001));\r\n\treturn rgb * RGB_TO_YUV;\r\n}\r\n\r\nvec3 yuv_to_rgb(vec3 yuv) {\r\n\tconst mat3 YUV_TO_RGB = mat3(vec3(1.0, 0.0, 1.13983), vec3(1.0, -0.39465, -0.58060), vec3(1.0, 2.03211, 0.0));\r\n\treturn clamp(yuv * YUV_TO_RGB, vec3(0.0), vec3(1.0));\r\n}\r</code></pre>\n</article>"
 }
